# Admin Architecture Rules

- Treat `docs/ADMIN_PORTAL_MASTER_SPEC.md` as the authoritative Level 1 specification.
- The admin portal is part of the existing GIPA Next.js application at `/admin`.
- Use the same PostgreSQL database.
- Preserve existing public application/contact functionality.
- Do not create a separate admin codebase or database for Level 1.
- Do not merge DriverApplication and WarehouseOperativeApplication.
- Do not duplicate applicant PII into admin metadata.
- Existing public UUID `id` values are the identity used by admin metadata FKs.
- Admin metadata must use explicit 1:1 relationships with unique foreign keys.
- Work phase-by-phase. Do not implement future phases without approval.
- If the repository conflicts with the specification, stop and report the conflict rather than silently redesigning.
